====================================================================================================
SUMMARY  --  C(t) = ||Cov_{mu_t}(grad S_W)||_op  on the four models
====================================================================================================
  model                        bounded?   integrable?   sup_t C_abs     L-uniform?   q(t)
  (1) single link SU(2)        YES         NO (sat.)     0.403062         n/a (1 link) exp, rate 3
  (2) 1D Dirichlet string      YES         NO (sat.)     lam_max<=4       YES         == 0 exactly
  (3) 2D YM tower              YES         NO (sat.)     0.40             YES         exp, rate E_1
  (4a) P4 U(1) one site        YES         NO (sat.)     (see above)      n/a          exp, rate 1
  (4b) P4 circulant ring       YES         NO (sat.)     4 EXACTLY        YES (p=0)   == 0 exactly

  Common law (all four):  C(0)=0 exactly;  C(t) rises like t;  C(t) -> ||E_nu[Hess S_W]||_op > 0.
  =>  sup_t C(t) < infinity  (branch (c))  but  int_0^inf C(t) dt = infinity (saturation).
  =>  the BD-relevant object is q(t)=||(Hess V_t)_-||_op = ||(E[Hess S_W] - Cov)_-||_op,
      whose integrability comes from the exact CANCELLATION of the two O(1) terms.

